# Member Engagement & Gamification (MEG-001)

**Purpose:** Define a **workspace-agnostic** member engagement platform for clubs. Engagement points encourage safe, useful participation. Points are **never** wallet balance or money.

---

## 1. Non-goals (V1)

| Rule | Rationale |
| ---- | --------- |
| No wallet / ledger coupling | Financial integrity |
| No public leaderboard | Avoid risky competition |
| No childish game chrome | Professional mountaineering tone |
| No payment-amount awards | Avoid pay-to-win |
| No difficulty-based awards | Safety — do not reward higher-risk climbs |
| No invented attendance/training awards without verifier | Only verifiable domain events |

---

## 2. Architecture layers

| Layer | Location | Responsibility |
| ----- | -------- | -------------- |
| **Engagement domain** | `apps/api/src/workspace-engagement/` | Profiles, immutable point events, badges, levels, award processors |
| **HTTP boundary** | `packages/engagement-http`, `engagement-http-contracts` | Route handlers, request/response contracts |
| **Capability gate** | Manifest `workspaceEngagement` + codegen bindings | Per-workspace enablement (Denali first) |
| **Member dashboard** | `apps/portal` BFF + widgets | Greeting, next tour, points, badges, wallet separation |
| **Operator overview** | `apps/web` engagement ops | Recent awards, member lookup, audit trail |
| **Denali presentation** | `packages/workspaces/denali` messages + manifest policy | Persian mountaineering copy, badge labels |

**WAC-001:** `apps/api` resolves engagement via generated bindings — no `workspaceType === "denali"` branches.

---

## 3. Data model

### 3.1 `engagement_profiles`

| Column | Type | Rule |
| ------ | ---- | ---- |
| `id` | UUID | PK |
| `tenant_id` | UUID | RLS scope |
| `workspace_id` | text | Workspace plugin id |
| `user_id` | UUID | Member |
| `total_points` | int | Derived cache; sum of non-reversed events |
| `current_level_code` | text | From manifest level thresholds |
| `created_at` / `updated_at` | timestamptz | |

**Unique:** `(tenant_id, workspace_id, user_id)`

### 3.2 `engagement_point_events` (immutable ledger)

| Column | Type | Rule |
| ------ | ---- | ---- |
| `id` | UUID | PK |
| `tenant_id` | UUID | RLS |
| `workspace_id` | text | |
| `user_id` | UUID | Recipient |
| `points_delta` | int | Positive award or negative correction |
| `source_module` | text | `identity`, `booking`, `engagement` |
| `source_event_type` | text | e.g. `profile.completed`, `registration.first_approved` |
| `source_entity_id` | UUID? | Registration id, etc. |
| `dedupe_key` | text | Stable idempotency key |
| `reverses_event_id` | UUID? | Correction links to original |
| `actor_user_id` | UUID? | Operator for manual correction |
| `actor_role` | text? | |
| `reason` | text? | Audit note |
| `created_at` | timestamptz | Insert-only |

**Unique:** `(tenant_id, dedupe_key)`

**RLS:** `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` on all engagement tables; queries require `tenant_id` from auth context.

---

## 4. V1 award rules (verifiable only)

| Rule | Trigger | Points | Dedupe key pattern |
| ---- | ------- | ------ | ------------------ |
| Profile complete | All manifest `memberProfile` required fields filled after PATCH `/identity/me` | 50 | `engagement:profile.completed:{userId}` |
| First approved registration | First `registration.approved` outbox for user in workspace | 100 | `engagement:registration.first_approved:{userId}` |

Badges (manifest-defined):

| Badge code | Earned when |
| ---------- | ----------- |
| `trailhead_ready` | `profile.completed` award posted |
| `first_expedition` | `registration.first_approved` award posted |
| `summit_rookie` | `total_points >= 100` |
| `ridge_partner` | `total_points >= 250` |

Levels (Denali V1):

| Code | Min points |
| ---- | ---------- |
| `base_camp` | 0 |
| `trail_member` | 100 |
| `summit_circle` | 250 |

---

## 5. HTTP API

### 5.1 Member routes

| Method | Path | Scope |
| ------ | ---- | ----- |
| GET | `/engagement/me/summary` | Member dashboard aggregate |
| GET | `/engagement/me/points` | Point event history |
| GET | `/engagement/me/badges` | Earned badges + progress |

### 5.2 Operator routes — member operations

| Method | Path | Scope |
| ------ | ---- | ----- |
| GET | `/engagement/operator/overview` | Recent awards + badge activity |
| GET | `/engagement/operator/members/:userId` | Member engagement lookup |
| POST | `/engagement/operator/members/:userId/adjust` | Manual point award or deduction (idempotent, reason required) |
| POST | `/engagement/operator/members/:userId/reverse` | Compensating reversal of a specific positive event (idempotent) |

### 5.3 Operator routes — definition management (V1.1)

Persisted per `(tenant_id, workspace_id)` with RLS, optimistic `row_version`, and append-only audit log.

| Method | Path | Scope |
| ------ | ---- | ----- |
| GET | `/engagement/operator/badges` | List badge definitions (incl. archived when `includeArchived`) |
| POST | `/engagement/operator/badges` | Create badge (idempotent POST) |
| PATCH | `/engagement/operator/badges/:code` | Edit localized copy, icon, trigger, activate/deactivate/archive |
| GET | `/engagement/operator/levels` | List level definitions |
| POST | `/engagement/operator/levels` | Create level |
| PATCH | `/engagement/operator/levels/:code` | Edit thresholds and status |
| GET | `/engagement/operator/award-rules` | List award rules (all versions) |
| POST | `/engagement/operator/award-rules` | Create new rule version |
| PATCH | `/engagement/operator/award-rules/:ruleId` | Edit / activate / deactivate with effective dates |
| GET | `/engagement/operator/audit-log` | Definition mutation audit trail |
| GET | `/engagement/operator/catalog` | Approved icons + supported domain events |
| GET | `/engagement/operator/policy` | Legacy aggregate snapshot (`managementMode: operator_managed`) |

**Permissions:** `owner` and `admin` may mutate definitions and member points; `viewer` is read-only (GET allowed, POST/PATCH denied).

**Award rule allowlist (V1):** only `profile.completed` (identity) and `registration.first_approved` (booking). Forbidden: wallet, payment, finance, or invented event names.

**Immutability:** `engagement_point_events` and earned `member_engagement_badges` rows are never deleted; definition archive disables future awards only.

---

## 6. Notifications (MNI-001)

Badge-earned events enqueue `member_notifications` with:

- `source_module`: `engagement`
- `entity_type`: `engagement_event`
- `event_type`: `engagement.badge.earned`
- `dedupe_key`: domain event id or stable badge award key

---

## 7. Testing matrix

| Suite | Proves |
| ----- | ------ |
| `engagement-persistence.postgres.spec.ts` | RLS, dedupe, cross-tenant denial |
| `engagement-awards.postgres.spec.ts` | Profile + registration award idempotency + outbox dispatch |
| Operator E2E | Member search (name/phone), policy catalog, adjust/reverse workflows |
| `engagement-http-boundary.spec.ts` | Contract parsing |
| Portal E2E | Dashboard renders points/badges separate from wallet |
| Web E2E | Operator overview + permissions |

